<Base title="Keynote writing in your voice" description="Develop a keynote with Loren Michaels Harris, from audience discovery and narrative structure to drafting, revisions, and optional rehearsal."><PageIntro title="Your ideas. Your voice. The right words." eyebrow="KEYNOTE WRITING / YOUR MESSAGE" description="For leaders and speakers preparing an important talk. Bring an idea, a set of notes, or an early draft. Build a keynote your audience can follow—and recognize as yours."><a class="button" href="/contact/?service=keynote-writing">Discuss your keynote ↗</a></PageIntro><section class="section wrap split"><div><p class="eyebrow">GIVE THE MESSAGE A THROUGH-LINE</p><h2>What do you want<br/>them to carry<br/><span class="gold-text">out of the room?</span></h2></div><div><p>A strong keynote needs a clear idea, a structure that holds it together, and language that sounds like the person delivering it.</p><p>The writing conversation begins with your audience and occasion. From there, the work moves through narrative structure, a draft, and an agreed revision process.</p><p>Rehearsal support can be discussed separately. Timelines, revision rounds, confidentiality, and ownership terms are confirmed before work begins.</p></div></section><section class="section dark"><div class="wrap"><p class="eyebrow">FROM DISCOVERY TO DELIVERY</p><h2>Build the talk.<br/>One clear step at a time.</h2><div class="steps">{[['Discovery','Clarify your audience, occasion, purpose, and starting material.'],['Narrative','Find the central idea and the stories that support it.'],['Draft','Develop the structure into a complete spoken message.'],['Revisions','Refine the draft through the feedback process agreed for your project.'],['Optional rehearsal','Discuss support for bringing the written words into the room.']].map(([title,body],i)=><article class="step"><span class="number">0{i+1}</span><h3>{title}</h3><p>{body}</p></article>)}</div></div></section><section class="section wrap split"><div><p class="eyebrow">LET’S GET SPECIFIC</p><h2>Tell us about<br/>the occasion.</h2></div><div><p>Include the audience, talk length, deadline, and any notes or draft you already have. That context helps define the work.</p><a class="button" href="/contact/?service=keynote-writing">Discuss your keynote ↗</a></div></section></Base>
